.SH "Typedef Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "typedef bool(* stumpless_filter_func_t) (const struct \fBstumpless_target\fP *target, const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP *entry)"

.PP
A function that determines whether a given entry should be sent to a given target\&. The two parameters are guaranteed not to be NULL whenever a filter function is called by the library itself, and so NULL checks are not necessary\&.
.PP
Note that this function does not actually add the entry to the target, but only evaluates whether or not it should be sent\&.
.PP
The safety attributes (thread, async, async-cancel) of a filter function come into play whenever an entry is sent to a target via stumpless_add_entry or another function that results in a call to this\&. If the function is not safe in conditions where the add function is, the target will need to be treated as though it is also unsafe in these conditions when entries are passed to it\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The target that the entry will be sent to if it passes\&. Will not be NULL when called during logging\&.
.br
\fIentry\fP The entry that is being submitted to the target\&. Will not be NULL when called during logging\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if the entry should be sent to the target, false if not\&. 
.RE
.PP

