.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int stumpless_add_entry (struct \fBstumpless_target\fP * target, const struct \fBstumpless_entry\fP * entry)"

.PP
Adds an entry into a given target\&. This is the primary logging function of stumpless; all other logging functions call this one after performing any setup specific to themselves\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe env locale\fP This function is thread safe\&. Different target types handle thread safety differently, as some require per-target locks and others can rely on system libraries to log safely, but all targets support thread safe logging in some manner\&. For target-specific information on how thread safety is supported and whether AS or AC safety can be assumed, refer to the documentation for the target's header file (in the \fCstumpless/target\fP include folder)\&. For all targets, the environment variables and locale will be used during some of the string formatting of the message\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from signal handlers as some targets make use of non-reentrant locks to coordinate access\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Unsafe lock\fP This function is not safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled, due to the use of locks in some targets that could be left locked\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItarget\fP The target to send the message to\&.
.br
\fIentry\fP The entry to send to the target\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A non-negative value if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then a negative value is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. If the entry was rejected by the target's filter, then 0 is returned\&. 
.RE
.PP

