\fIsubs\fP Substitutions for any format specifiers provided in message\&. The number of substitutions provided must exactly match the number of specifiers given\&. This list must be started via \fCva_start\fP before being used, and \fCva_end\fP should be called afterwards, as this function does not call it\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A non-negative value if no error is encountered\&. If an error is encountered, then a negative value is returned and an error code is set appropriately\&. If the entry was rejected by the target's filter, then 0 is returned\&. 
.RE
.PP

